            <ArticleTitle>Pain as a learned response: a review of behavioral factors in chronic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>881-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This review of the literature on pain behavior suggests that learning factors may have a critical role in shaping an individual's response to pain. Understanding these pain behaviors becomes especially helpful in diagnosis and treatment of patients with chronic pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
